---
description: Value mappings — dictionaries for renaming and normalizing values in widgets
globs: dashboards/**/*.yaml
alwaysApply: false
---

<rule>
<meta>
  This rule covers value mapping dictionaries that rename raw values to human-readable labels in widget columns.
  Activate when defining `mappings:` blocks or referencing mappings in column definitions.
</meta>

<schema>
  <mapping_definition>
    ```yaml
    mappings:
      languages:
        entries:
          arabic: AR
          english: EN
          french: FR
          german: DE
          spanish: ES
          russian: RU
          unknown: ""
        fallback: original                  # Keep original if no match

      media_sources:
        entries:
          Facebook_abakus: FB_A
          Facebook Ads: FB
          googleadwords_int: GA
          TikTok: TT
          True organic: Org

      platforms:
        entries:
          ios: iOS
          android: Android
          web: Web
    ```
  </mapping_definition>

  <fallback_behavior>
    ```yaml
    # Keep original value if not in entries
    fallback: original

    # Use a fixed default string
    fallback:
      default: "Unknown"

    # No fallback (omit field) = show original value as-is
    ```
  </fallback_behavior>

  <mapping_reference>
    In rich_table column definitions:
    ```yaml
    columns:
      - id: language
        label: Lang
        type: dimension
        mapping: { id: languages }

      - id: payment_source
        label: Payment
        type: dimension
        mapping: { id: platforms, fallback: { default: "Other" } }
    ```
  </mapping_reference>
</schema>

<examples>
  <in_projection_columns>
    ```yaml
    projections:
      daily_costs_by_source:
        sql: |
          SELECT media_source, SUM(costs) as costs
          FROM {{source:total_by_ad}}
          GROUP BY 1
        columns:
          media_source: { type: string, description: "Media source", mapping: media_sources }
    ```
  </in_projection_columns>

  <normalize>
    Independent of mappings, columns can normalize text casing:
    ```yaml
    - id: plan_name
      label: Type
      type: dimension
      normalize: capitalize               # capitalize | uppercase | lowercase
    ```
    - `capitalize`: "max" → "Max"
    - `uppercase`: "max" → "MAX"
    - `lowercase`: "MAX" → "max"
  </normalize>

  <shared_mappings>
    In `_shared/_mappings.yaml` (flat dict):
    ```yaml
    languages:
      entries:
        english: EN
        russian: RU
      fallback: original
    ```
    Merge: dashboard `_shared/` is base; tab mappings override on key conflict.
  </shared_mappings>
</examples>

<rules>
  <hard_constraints>
    - Mapping key lookup is **case-insensitive** at runtime (keys normalized to lowercase)
    - Mappings are applied at render time, not in SQL
    - Use `fallback: original` to pass through unmapped values unchanged
    - Mappings are defined once at dashboard level and reused across all widgets
    - Per-column `fallback` in mapping ref overrides the mapping definition's fallback
  </hard_constraints>
</rules>

<see_also>
  - `dashboard-rich-table` — column mapping references, normalize
  - `dashboard-yaml-structure` — shared mappings, merge hierarchy
</see_also>
</rule>
